WEBVTT

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:08.650
<b>Meiji Tokyo Renka</b>

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:39.150
Goodbye...

00:01:49.350 --> 00:01:50.790
Goodbye.

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:00.630
Good—

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:07.520
<b>Meiji Tokyo Renka</b>

00:02:15.630 --> 00:02:19.080
So, have you heard about that café  
they introduced on TV yesterday?

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:21.590
Oh, I saw that. It's near here, isn't it?

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:23.630
Their desserts should be 
half-price right now.

00:02:23.630 --> 00:02:24.810
Why don't we go check it out?

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:25.880
I'll totally go.

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:26.880
I definitely want to go!

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:28.150
Let's do it!

00:02:29.130 --> 00:02:34.460
<i>I used to laugh like that a lot.</i>

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:39.760
Happy Birthday Mei-chan!

00:02:40.610 --> 00:02:42.180
Blow out the candles, Mei-chan!

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:42.610
One big blow!

00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:43.040
Okay!

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:45.290
Yay!

00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:49.050
Okay, time for Mei's favorite dish, 
roast beef.

00:02:49.990 --> 00:02:52.250
I love roast beef!

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:56.260
You're so funny, Mei-chan.

00:02:58.730 --> 00:03:02.570
<i>But that's when the fun ended.</i>

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:07.570
Cake? I like cake too, 
but I like beef even more!

00:03:07.570 --> 00:03:11.320
What about you? Oh, you do? Really?

00:03:11.910 --> 00:03:14.990
Hey, Mei-chan, who are you talking to?

00:03:14.990 --> 00:03:17.020
Huh? My friends.

00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:18.980
Y-Your friends?

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:20.330
Where are they?

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:22.050
They're right here, see?

00:03:22.050 --> 00:03:23.780
Can't you hear them talking?

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:27.100
You want to join in? Okay, sure.

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:30.040
You do, too? Of course, what's your name?

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:31.970
I see, I see. Really?

00:03:31.970 --> 00:03:33.660
It's okay, right?

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:35.080
M-M-Mei-chan!

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:37.250
G-G-Ghosts?

00:03:39.950 --> 00:03:42.790
I heard that Mei-chan can hear ghosts talking.

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:50.260
Did you know? Apparently, that girl
 can see ghosts.

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:51.700
Whoa, really?

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:53.130
Mei-chan!

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:57.640
<i>I never realized nobody 
else could hear them.</i>

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:54.410
Mei-chan!

00:03:54.410 --> 00:03:55.880
Hey, Mei-chan!

00:03:56.660 --> 00:03:58.120
Talk to us!

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:00.710
Mei-chan, Mei-chan!

00:04:02.710 --> 00:04:05.200
<i>I've been alone ever since.</i>

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:08.630
<i>Yes, it's easier this way.</i>

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:12.110
Hey, isn't that girl in your class?
 We should invite her.

00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:14.270
You're Ayazuki Mei-san, right?

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:15.340
Do you wanna come with us?

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:16.650
Hang on a second!

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:23.020
Oh, I'll have to pass.

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:25.080
But thank you.

00:04:25.650 --> 00:04:27.650
Y-You sure?

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:29.960
Forget about her.

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:31.170
She's always by herself.

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:32.520
She seems to like it that way.

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:34.560
Huh? Really?

00:04:36.370 --> 00:04:39.450
She's been able to hear ghosts
talking since we were kids.

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:41.740
Is that true? That's pretty amazing.

00:04:41.740 --> 00:04:43.220
Amazing?

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:45.160
Never mind that, cake!

00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:47.160
Yeah, that's right!

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:56.680
Mei-chan...

00:04:58.190 --> 00:04:59.350
Mei-chan.

00:05:02.370 --> 00:05:03.620
Mei-chan.

00:05:24.710 --> 00:05:26.470
Now then, ladies and gentlemen!

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:32.170
The light of the Strawberry Moon 
shines bewitchingly on this night.

00:05:32.170 --> 00:05:34.710
I invite you all to a mysterious 
world in this great magical show,

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:39.100
brought to you by a master of Western magic!

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:46.330
Behold, this box is an 
incredibly mysterious one

00:05:46.330 --> 00:05:49.040
that makes everything that 
goes into it disappear.

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:54.200
I will show you how it can make 
anything disappear at once,

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:56.860
be it an elephant, tank, or airplane.

00:05:57.190 --> 00:06:02.880
Of course, that includes any of you who 
wish to be anywhere but here.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:08.080
Now, is there anyone here who might 
wish to step inside the box?

00:06:08.810 --> 00:06:12.150
Perhaps you there, young lady.

00:06:16.570 --> 00:06:17.970
What do you say?

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:25.000
Young lady, I insist.

00:06:30.140 --> 00:06:34.420
Now then, allow me to show 
you how this young lady

00:06:34.420 --> 00:06:38.300
will completely disappear once 
I count down from three.

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:42.320
<i>How did I get roped into this?</i>

00:06:42.830 --> 00:06:46.290
<i>I really hate being the center of attention.</i>

00:06:47.710 --> 00:06:51.710
What fate will befall 
this courageous young lady?

00:06:51.710 --> 00:06:55.120
Please give a round of applause 
when she successfully disappears.

00:06:57.490 --> 00:06:58.820
<i>For some reason...</i>

00:07:00.890 --> 00:07:04.720
<i>I feel rather at peace.</i>

00:07:05.030 --> 00:07:06.110
Three...

00:07:07.510 --> 00:07:08.610
two...

00:07:10.270 --> 00:07:11.340
one!

00:07:29.860 --> 00:07:32.760
<b>The Unexpected Strawberry Moon</b>

00:08:09.860 --> 00:08:10.690
Huh?

00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:14.800
Wha—?

00:08:15.310 --> 00:08:16.470
Why?

00:08:17.110 --> 00:08:19.430
Eh? Huh? Eh?

00:08:21.320 --> 00:08:22.820
What?!

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:40.870
What's wrong?!

00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:49.610
Are you all right? Are you hurt?

00:08:50.510 --> 00:08:53.890
I-I'm fine.

00:08:54.460 --> 00:08:55.770
Let me take a look.

00:09:00.740 --> 00:09:02.690
Are you in any pain?

00:09:02.690 --> 00:09:04.470
I-I'm not.

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:08.380
You seem all right.

00:09:10.050 --> 00:09:10.970
Yes.

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:15.320
What's this?

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:18.420
Oh, these are my headphones.

00:09:18.420 --> 00:09:19.710
Headphones?

00:09:19.710 --> 00:09:21.550
She appears to be unharmed.

00:09:21.550 --> 00:09:22.430
Yes.

00:09:35.750 --> 00:09:36.570
Come now.

00:09:50.690 --> 00:09:54.680
Nevertheless, you are wearing 
quite reasonable clothing.

00:09:54.680 --> 00:09:55.540
Huh?

00:09:56.220 --> 00:09:59.630
It's a simple design using the 
minimum fabric necessary.

00:09:59.630 --> 00:10:03.340
A style that emphasizes only functionality, 
without being inclined to extravagance.

00:10:03.340 --> 00:10:07.530
I would say it is truly innovative, 
no, almost revolutionary.

00:10:07.530 --> 00:10:08.940
Ougai-san...

00:10:10.230 --> 00:10:11.830
Oh, pardon me.

00:10:12.780 --> 00:10:14.280
Where do you live?

00:10:14.950 --> 00:10:18.390
Unfortunately, we both have somewhere 
we need to be shortly.

00:10:18.390 --> 00:10:21.400
However, afterward, I can have you taken
 home in this, if you wish.

00:10:24.250 --> 00:10:25.690
A carriage?!

00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:30.310
No, honestly, I'll be fine.

00:10:30.310 --> 00:10:32.250
Thank you very much though.

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:33.670
You will not be fine.

00:10:34.510 --> 00:10:36.440
Please feel free to ride with us.

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:40.320
We cannot just look the other way 
and let you go off on your own like this.

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:41.080
Come along.

00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:43.070
But I...

00:10:43.070 --> 00:10:46.680
If you would rather be attacked by 
stray dogs, then we won't stop you.

00:10:47.070 --> 00:10:51.080
N-No, I can get home on my own. I—

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:53.240
<i>Huh? Home?</i>

00:10:54.070 --> 00:10:59.360
Uh, where is my home, anyway?

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:02.560
More importantly, where am I?

00:11:04.360 --> 00:11:06.160
I-I don't know.

00:11:06.160 --> 00:11:08.610
Huh? What's happened to me?

00:11:10.610 --> 00:11:11.890
You don't know?

00:11:13.470 --> 00:11:17.100
When I woke up, I was just lying here.

00:11:17.100 --> 00:11:18.800
Should we take her to the hospital?

00:11:22.390 --> 00:11:24.850
No, there's no problem here.

00:11:26.130 --> 00:11:28.110
Then, perhaps the police?

00:11:29.660 --> 00:11:31.890
No. Would you like to come with us?

00:11:31.890 --> 00:11:34.160
With you?

00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:47.150
<i>A carriage... I'm seriously 
riding in a carriage right now.</i>

00:11:47.150 --> 00:11:49.370
What is your name, young lady?

00:11:50.330 --> 00:11:53.860
My name is... Huh?  What is my name?

00:11:55.890 --> 00:11:59.320
Oh, pardon my rudeness.
My name is Mori Rintaro.

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:01.150
I serve as an army surgeon.

00:12:01.150 --> 00:12:02.870
A-Army surgeon?

00:12:02.870 --> 00:12:05.340
Syunso, you should introduce 
yourself as well.

00:12:05.340 --> 00:12:08.100
I'm Hishida. Hishida Syunso.

00:12:08.100 --> 00:12:10.830
Hishida Syunso-san.

00:12:12.210 --> 00:12:14.070
It's very nice to meet you.

00:12:14.410 --> 00:12:16.350
Syunso is an art student.

00:12:16.930 --> 00:12:19.950
He is the darling of the Japanese art world.

00:12:21.640 --> 00:12:24.180
What is your name, young lady?

00:12:24.460 --> 00:12:27.340
Oh, right, my name is...

00:12:28.210 --> 00:12:29.480
Mei.

00:12:29.480 --> 00:12:30.420
Huh?

00:12:31.050 --> 00:12:34.510
Mei. Ayazuki Mei.

00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:40.190
A-Ayazuki Mei.

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:44.440
At least you remember your own name.

00:12:47.530 --> 00:12:49.430
<i>What was that voice just now?</i>

00:12:58.650 --> 00:13:00.280
<i>Where am I?</i>

00:13:02.350 --> 00:13:05.590
Behold. We will be arriving shortly.

00:13:29.920 --> 00:13:31.140
What is this?

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:33.340
The festivities this evening are 
being hosted by Inoue Kaoru,

00:13:33.340 --> 00:13:35.040
the Minister of Foreign Affairs,

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:38.470
because the Crown Prince of Russia, 
Nicholas II, is visiting Japan.

00:13:38.470 --> 00:13:41.000
T-The crown prince of Russia?

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:42.970
Umm... Where are we?

00:13:42.970 --> 00:13:44.600
The Rokumeikan.

00:13:44.600 --> 00:13:46.030
The Rokumeikan?

00:13:46.630 --> 00:13:48.210
I've heard of it before.

00:13:48.210 --> 00:13:52.730
<i>But wait... Does the Rokumeikan still exist?</i>

00:13:52.730 --> 00:13:55.240
Look, the crown prince is over there.

00:13:55.240 --> 00:13:57.600
The politicians are swarming around him.

00:13:59.260 --> 00:14:01.260
Ougai-san, are you sure about this?

00:14:01.260 --> 00:14:02.980
About what, Syunso?

00:14:02.980 --> 00:14:08.140
Bringing a lady that is dressed so strangely 
to a party at the Rokumeikan?

00:14:08.700 --> 00:14:10.590
S-Strangely?

00:14:10.590 --> 00:14:12.150
What is with that girl?

00:14:12.490 --> 00:14:14.240
She's wearing such vulgar attire.

00:14:14.240 --> 00:14:16.970
She's utterly shameful,
exposing her legs like that.

00:14:18.870 --> 00:14:20.370
It'll be fine.

00:14:20.820 --> 00:14:24.030
Now, Little Squirrel, 
enjoy yourself to the fullest.

00:14:24.030 --> 00:14:25.370
Little Squirrel?

00:14:26.640 --> 00:14:28.000
Little Squirrel.

00:14:28.630 --> 00:14:30.770
Okay...

00:14:30.770 --> 00:14:32.560
<i>Why is he calling me that?</i>

00:14:32.560 --> 00:14:35.650
<i>And he expects me to enjoy 
myself to the fullest?</i>

00:14:36.280 --> 00:14:37.770
<i>How, though?</i>

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:43.660
Th-That's the smell of roast beef!

00:14:43.660 --> 00:14:47.370
Oh? So you like roast beef, Little Squirrel?

00:14:47.370 --> 00:14:49.920
You should eat as much as you'd like, then.

00:14:49.920 --> 00:14:51.980
You are welcome to eat whatever—

00:14:51.980 --> 00:14:53.040
Ougai-san.

00:14:53.910 --> 00:14:54.960
She's over there.

00:14:57.150 --> 00:14:58.930
Pardon me.

00:14:59.670 --> 00:15:01.460
Pardon me.

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:04.800
Roast beef, roast beef.

00:15:02.270 --> 00:15:04.100
Pardon me.

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:09.600
I'm so sorry!

00:15:17.570 --> 00:15:22.310
I-I don't know who has touched 
this dish, and now it's touching me!

00:15:24.310 --> 00:15:29.560
Honestly, Kyoka-chan, your 
germophobia is such a pain.

00:15:33.080 --> 00:15:34.430
Kawakami...

00:15:34.430 --> 00:15:36.820
And I told you not to call me Kyoka-chan!

00:15:36.820 --> 00:15:41.030
Well, then, Izumi Kyoka-sensei, 
when is it going to be ready?

00:15:41.030 --> 00:15:42.860
Your next play, that is.

00:15:42.860 --> 00:15:43.890
Shut up!

00:15:44.970 --> 00:15:46.160
A rabbit?

00:15:46.160 --> 00:15:49.730
Hey, you! Don't get so 
close to me, would you?

00:15:49.730 --> 00:15:53.060
I really hate it when someone 
I don't know gets close to me.

00:15:53.870 --> 00:15:55.730
Pay him no mind.

00:15:55.730 --> 00:15:58.220
Kyoka-chan is an extreme germophobe.

00:15:58.220 --> 00:15:59.610
Stop calling me Kyoka-chan!

00:15:59.610 --> 00:16:02.860
But this is my first time meeting 
such an assertive woman.

00:16:03.620 --> 00:16:07.860
You went through all this just because 
you wanted to dance with me, didn't you?

00:16:07.860 --> 00:16:09.110
Hang on...

00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:10.750
The nerve of this girl!

00:16:10.750 --> 00:16:13.530
I am supposed to dance the 
next song with Otojiro-sama!

00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:15.860
You have to wait your turn.

00:16:15.860 --> 00:16:17.950
We're all in line, you know.

00:16:17.950 --> 00:16:20.430
Why don't you go back 
to the end of the line?

00:16:20.430 --> 00:16:22.870
What's with her disgraceful clothing?

00:16:22.870 --> 00:16:24.740
No, you've got it all wrong.

00:16:24.740 --> 00:16:27.920
I was just following the 
scent of the roast beef.

00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:30.460
And there was a rabbit on his shoulder...

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:31.390
A rabbit?

00:16:32.880 --> 00:16:34.850
Where is this rabbit?

00:16:34.850 --> 00:16:37.640
It's right there, on his shoulder.

00:16:38.620 --> 00:16:41.290
Kyoka-chan certainly does like rabbits.

00:16:41.290 --> 00:16:42.720
Don't call me that!

00:16:42.720 --> 00:16:46.400
But he wouldn't bring a 
rabbit ornament here.

00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:50.410
No, it's not an ornament. 
It's more fluffy-like.

00:16:48.690 --> 00:16:50.400
<b>Fluffy</b>

00:16:51.380 --> 00:16:54.920
Are you sure you didn't just 
see a ghost or something?

00:16:55.410 --> 00:16:57.160
A ghost?

00:16:57.160 --> 00:17:00.400
Did you mention ghosts just now?

00:17:07.080 --> 00:17:10.350
Thank you for such an 
enjoyable moment, madame.

00:17:10.350 --> 00:17:12.150
I hope you continue to 
have a pleasant evening.

00:17:12.150 --> 00:17:15.790
Apologies for the delay. I am Lafcadio Hearn,

00:17:15.790 --> 00:17:19.600
a teacher of English literature 
at Tokyo Imperial University.

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:22.150
And this is my Japanese name.

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:24.440
<b>Tokyo Imperial 
University Instructor 
Japanese Folklore
 Researcher</b>

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:24.440
<b>Koizumi 
Yakumo</b>

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:27.050
Koizumi Yakumo?

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:29.830
Like the man who wrote the 
tales of Hoichi the Earless?

00:17:29.830 --> 00:17:32.440
My, so you have heard of me?

00:17:32.440 --> 00:17:35.710
That pleases me immensely.

00:17:35.710 --> 00:17:39.310
Well... I believe the name of 
the novelist who put together

00:17:39.310 --> 00:17:42.760
that collection ghost stories 
was Koizumi Yakumo, but...

00:17:42.760 --> 00:17:46.210
Huh? Did you say that's you? Wha?

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:49.110
A researcher of Japanese folklore, eh?

00:17:49.110 --> 00:17:51.630
I am Kawakami Otojiro. Nice to meet you.

00:17:51.630 --> 00:17:53.420
I am familiar with you.

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:56.810
You are the up-and-coming stage actor.

00:17:56.810 --> 00:17:59.230
By the way, Miss...

00:17:59.230 --> 00:18:02.840
May I have the pleasure of dancing 
with you, mademoiselle?

00:18:02.840 --> 00:18:04.230
Hold on, umm...

00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:08.510
Now then, please do continue with
the topic you were discussing earlier.

00:18:05.370 --> 00:18:10.220
Umm, umm, umm, umm, umm...

00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:14.020
That man!

00:18:14.020 --> 00:18:15.480
Oh, miss!

00:18:16.500 --> 00:18:18.030
Hey, you!

00:18:19.030 --> 00:18:22.550
Well, hello there, young lady. 
So this is where you've been?

00:18:22.550 --> 00:18:25.500
I've been looking for you 
for quite some time.

00:18:25.980 --> 00:18:29.410
Since there is a party here this evening,

00:18:29.410 --> 00:18:33.250
I thought you might be wandering 
around here somewhere.

00:18:33.250 --> 00:18:35.610
I'm glad you seem 
to be enjoying yourself.

00:18:35.610 --> 00:18:37.450
Enjoying myself?

00:18:37.450 --> 00:18:38.550
Will you have some?

00:18:38.550 --> 00:18:39.520
Of course!

00:18:39.750 --> 00:18:44.230
Nevermind about that, what happened 
to me when you did that trick?

00:18:44.230 --> 00:18:46.600
I went into the box...

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:51.770
I went in, and when I woke up,
I was in an unfamiliar park.

00:18:51.770 --> 00:18:55.520
I can't remember all kinds 
of things, like where my own home is.

00:18:55.520 --> 00:18:58.160
It's not surprising that you're confused.

00:18:58.770 --> 00:19:01.250
Honestly, even I was surprised.

00:19:01.250 --> 00:19:04.790
I call myself an extraordinary magician,

00:19:04.790 --> 00:19:07.940
but even I didn't think I could 
actually make a person disappear.

00:19:07.940 --> 00:19:08.790
Disappear?

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:13.030
Though it might be more accurate 
to say that I transported you.

00:19:13.030 --> 00:19:14.170
Transported me?

00:19:14.170 --> 00:19:18.290
Yes, from present day 
Tokyo to Meiji era Tokyo.

00:19:18.610 --> 00:19:22.050
Meiji era Tokyo?

00:19:22.050 --> 00:19:25.330
In other words, you traveled back in time.

00:19:25.330 --> 00:19:30.560
And the reason your memory is so fuzzy is because of an
accident that occurs when you travel through time.

00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:33.100
Time travel...

00:19:41.080 --> 00:19:44.720
Oh my, how terrible! The power went out.

00:19:50.390 --> 00:19:51.560
A fox?

00:20:00.150 --> 00:20:01.850
The piano is playing by itself!

00:20:01.850 --> 00:20:03.590
M-My cane!

00:20:06.840 --> 00:20:10.330
A ghost? No, it's just a mischievous fox.

00:20:10.330 --> 00:20:13.540
Oh, come on. It's just a fox.

00:20:13.540 --> 00:20:15.870
What a waste of my time.

00:20:15.870 --> 00:20:18.830
Thank goodness, he's going to catch it.

00:20:32.690 --> 00:20:33.980
Supernatural fox.

00:20:36.630 --> 00:20:37.640
No!

00:20:46.170 --> 00:20:48.640
Are you a Tamayori?

00:20:49.630 --> 00:20:50.700
Eh?

00:20:51.870 --> 00:20:54.700
You can see the ghosts.

00:20:55.880 --> 00:20:57.310
Tamayori?

00:21:03.410 --> 00:21:04.720
Huh?

00:21:07.730 --> 00:21:10.410
Answer me, girl. Who are you?

00:21:16.760 --> 00:21:18.870
It's all right, Little Squirrel.

00:21:22.780 --> 00:21:25.610
Could you please refrain from 
such violence, Inspector Fujita

00:21:25.610 --> 00:21:28.320
of the Metropolitan Police 
Department Supernatural Division?

00:21:29.180 --> 00:21:33.810
What are you trying to pull, 
Army Surgeon First Class?

00:21:34.460 --> 00:21:36.420
Or should I say, Mori Ougai-dono.

00:21:39.490 --> 00:21:43.030
<i>Mori Ougai?</i>

00:21:44.490 --> 00:21:46.830
I have a few questions for the girl.

00:21:47.660 --> 00:21:53.860
Please do not glower so severely 
at my precious fiancée.

00:21:57.190 --> 00:22:00.560
F-Fiancée?

00:22:08.250 --> 00:22:11.180
You belong to me.

00:22:18.040 --> 00:22:19.030
Isn't that right?

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:39.930
<b>Meiji Tokyo Renka</b>

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:39.930
Next Episode Preview

00:23:29.970 --> 00:23:39.930
Sukiyaki Is Romance Veiled in Steam

00:23:31.170 --> 00:23:33.380
How magnificent!

00:23:33.380 --> 00:23:35.730
I've never seen such a 
beautiful creature before.

00:23:35.730 --> 00:23:37.190
May I pet you?

00:23:37.990 --> 00:23:39.750
P-Pervert!
